    "knowledge/deploy.md": {
      "kind": "facts",
      "path": "knowledge/deploy.md",
      "name": "deploy",
      "description": "Deploy: how the hub and its previews go out.",
      "content": "Deploy: how the hub and its previews go out.\n\n- Preview ports are picked outside the kernel's ephemeral range (ruling 2026-10-19)\n  Why: a bind refused for its address said so\n- A start republishes every runtime file whose bytes changed since the last start, so a dashboard reload after an update reads the new bundle, the agent's sessions keep their old one until they restart, and a stale service worker never serves the previous build's chunks to anyone (since 2026-10-17, from n-20261017-100000-a7b8c9 n-20261017-110000-b8c9d0, used 2026-10-19)\n- The scratch hub listens on 127.0.0.1 only (since 2026-10-03, from n-20261003-090000-d4e5f6, used 2026-10-18)\n- Releases are cut from main every Tuesday (since 2026-10-03, from n-20261003-090000-d4e5f6, used 2026-10-16)\n\n## Formerly\n\n- The scratch hub's ports came from the ephemeral range (since 2026-10-02, until 2026-10-19, from n-20261003-090000-d4e5f6, replaced by n-20261019-100000-a1b2c3)\n",
      "prose": false,
      "chars": 946,
      "changedAt": 1792238400000,
      "marks": ["current", "current", "current", "current", "formerly"],
      "thresholds": {
        "archiveDays": 90,
